.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt VERIFY-BRIDGE.SH 8
.Os MANET
.Sh NAME
.Nm verify-bridge.sh
.Nd check the node's bridged end-user-device configuration
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
checks bridge and BATMAN membership, bridge IPv4 addresses, DHCP isolation,
dnsmasq configuration, multicast settings and recorded interface roles.
Run as root so BATMAN and firewall checks can read their state.
The command takes no options and does not repair configuration.
.Pp
Results and the summary use colored terminal output.
Errors and warnings go to standard error.
Warnings can be normal, such as an absent wired user device or a HaLow
interface still initializing.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/ap_interface , /var/lib/mesh_if , /var/lib/halow_if
Configured access-point and mesh interfaces.
.It Pa /etc/dnsmasq.d/mesh-eud.conf
Bridge DHCP configuration.
.It Pa /var/run/ethernet_detection_state
Recorded Ethernet role.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Returns the number of failed checks as its exit status.
Warnings alone return 0.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo verify-bridge.sh
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ethernet-autodetect.sh 8 ,
.Xr radio-setup.sh 8
